	spec: 'Web cards collapse only through their title/header disclosure control. Body taps never collapse open assistant replies, user prompts, thinking, tools, notices or queued messages, including taps that clear native text selection. Links and body controls retain their own actions. Closed compact rows without a separate header remain tappable to open. This replaces bp1 body-tap collapse and r4d unselected-output collapse; configured initial fold states, header open-state restoration and terminal controls remain unchanged. Regression checks cover phone touch and desktop clicks, selection clearing, and header collapse.',
